            <ArticleTitle>Food labeling: health claims; soluble dietary fiber from certain foods and coronary heart disease. Final rule.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44207-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is adopting as a final rule, without change, the provisions of the interim final rule that amended the regulation authorizing a health claim on the relationship between beta-glucan soluble fiber from whole oat sources and reduced risk of coronary heart disease (CHD). FDA is taking this action to complete the rulemaking initiated with the interim final rule.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
